/* The Board section of the EVN ALPHA sidebar: the live console, the port, the firmware version,
 * the battery, the motor ports, the servo ports, the two serial ports, the I2C devices and the
 * files on the board.
 *
 * The rows are not only a display: while the live console is connected each port can be driven from
 * its buttons (run a motor, drive a servo, colour an LED strip, change a sensor setting, read a
 * sensor four times a second in its own row, put the REPL on the Bluetooth module). Every one of
 * those goes through one `call` / `exec` / `watch` on the console; none of them is on a timer, and
 * none of them is offered when the console is not live - the buttons are hidden by the menus, and
 * the commands say so politely if they are reached another way.
 *
 * Where the numbers come from:
 *  - while the live console is connected (src/console.ts holds the port), the firmware version and
 *    the file list come from one `info` request and the battery and the motor angles from the
 *    telemetry the board sends four times a second. Nothing here opens the port itself.
 *  - otherwise (console off, paused by a program or the REPL, or the board busy with its own
 *    main.py) the old on-demand mpremote read is used, and only when nothing else holds the port:
 *    a read is refused while the EVN terminal has it and while the console is connecting, live or
 *    watching a running program.
 * Talking to the board is never done on a timer from here; the 10 s poll behind boardState() only
 * lists USB ports.
 */
